          <mxGeometry height="61" width="980" x="585" y="455" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4n21" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E6F4F1;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#172B4D;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;strokeWidth=0;" value="CONTROLLER CONFIGURATION&lt;br&gt;K: number of inputs per output; N: output count&lt;br&gt;IN_BASE, W_BASE, B_BASE, OUT_BASE&lt;br&gt;relu_enable; shift[4:0]; start / ack&lt;br&gt;K &amp;gt;= 1; N &amp;gt;= 1; all addresses in range.&lt;br&gt;Host preloads SRAM and configuration while idle.&lt;br&gt;Layer parameters and bias scales are prepared offline." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="735" x="35" y="600" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4n22" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F1F5FF;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#172B4D;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;strokeWidth=0;" value="LOOP AND LANE MAPPING&lt;br&gt;Start: n=0. Each pair: k=0; load biases.&lt;br&gt;For k = 0 .. K-1: fetch x[k], W[n][k], W[n+1][k];&lt;br&gt;then enable both MACs for one edge.&lt;br&gt;POST; STORE0; STORE1; n += 2.&lt;br&gt;If n+1 &amp;gt;= N: suppress lane-1 reads, updates and store.&lt;br&gt;done only after the final required SRAM write." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="230" width="765" x="800" y="600" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4n23" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F1F5FF;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#172B4D;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;strokeWidth=0;" value="NEXT-LAYER HANDOFF&lt;br&gt;Layer L reads A and writes B. After ALL outputs are stored, the next layer reads B and writes A. Update K_next = N_previous and select the next weights, biases and shift. A and B are separate address regions, not separate SRAM ports. They must each fit their assigned layer activations. This baseline runs one configured layer per start; host reconfigures before the next start." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="185" width="1530" x="35" y="865" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4n24" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF4E5;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#172B4D;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;strokeWidth=0;" value="SCOPE AND LIMITS&lt;br&gt;This is a cycle-defined architectural specification, not a synthesized or RTL-validated implementation. No AXI, DMA, instruction fetch, SRAM stalls, or overlapping reads/writes are assumed. The Result FIFO block is specified as a depth-1 output hold stage: two simultaneous results (q0, q1 plus valid bits) are captured explicitly, then written separately.&lt;br&gt;For layers larger than allocated SRAM regions: software must provide tiles and transfers. Preserve 32-bit partial sums across input tiles; apply activation only after the complete dot product. Autonomous tiling / external-memory transfer is not implemented here.&lt;br&gt;Clock period must satisfy operand register -&amp;gt; multiplier -&amp;gt; 32-bit adder -&amp;gt; accumulator setup, and POST combinational timing. Adding pipeline stages changes the schedule." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="1530" x="35" y="1080" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
