        <mxCell id="p6n29" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="M24 = 680,  M33 = -130,  M42 = 28" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="660" x="905" y="465" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n30" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="E11 / C6" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="110" x="35" y="500" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n31" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="MAC34, MAC43 fire. Row 3 done: h3+b3" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="760" x="145" y="500" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n32" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="M34 = -290,  M43 = 88" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="660" x="905" y="500" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n33" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="E12 / C7" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="110" x="35" y="535" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n34" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="MAC44 fires. Row 4 done: h4+b4" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="760" x="145" y="535" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n35" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="M44 = 88" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="660" x="905" y="535" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n36" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="E13" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="110" x="35" y="570" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n37" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="POST: ReLU → INT64 multiply by M → ties-even shift → FIFO capture" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="760" x="145" y="570" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n38" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="q = 76, 127, 0, 22" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="660" x="905" y="570" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n39" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="E14" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="110" x="35" y="605" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n40" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="STORE: write q in low32, byte-enable=0x000F; pop FIFO; DONE" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="760" x="145" y="605" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n41" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="word = 0x16007F4C" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="660" x="905" y="605" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n42" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#F1F5FF;strokeColor=none;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;strokeWidth=0;" value="DIRECT DATAPATH / CONTROL&lt;br&gt;SRAM Q[127:0] connects directly to the 16 PE weight registers and to local bias/x/config capture registers. The sequencer supplies addresses, RD/WR enables, destination tags and capture strobes; payload does not pass through CPU scalar registers or an extra fetch/copy pipeline. A registered SRAM read needs latency-matched capture; subsequent reads may already be in progress. During C1..C7, x moves down and psum moves right over dedicated registered links. MAC(r,c) fires at C(r+c-1). A row starts from its INT32 bias and holds its completed sum until POST." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="1530" x="35" y="670" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n43" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#F1F5FF;strokeColor=none;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;strokeWidth=0;" value="128-BIT MEMORY FORMAT — BYTE ADDRESSES&lt;br&gt;A=0x0000; W1=0x0100; W2=0x0110; B1=0x0200; B2=0x0210; hidden B=0x0300; CFG1=0x0400; CFG2=0x0410. Every object starts on a 16-byte boundary. W line: byte[4*r+c]=W[r][c], zero-based r/c. Bias line: four INT32 lanes. CFG: [31:0]=M, [63:32]=S, [95:64]=flags (bit0=ReLU), upper32 reserved. X/q vector uses bits31:0, four INT8 bytes LSB first. STORE enables only low 4 bytes. Logical SRAM=1024x128=16 KiB." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1530" x="35" y="840" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n44" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#FFF4E5;strokeColor=none;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;strokeWidth=0;" value="TIMING ASSUMPTIONS / BANDWIDTH&lt;br&gt;Assume one-cycle SRAM response, one new 128-bit request per clock, no stalls, and byte-write enables. Four reads issue E1..E4; destinations capture E2..E5. Then C1..C7 at E6..E12; POST E13; STORE E14. Two sequential cold layers take 28 edges, excluding command acceptance/preloading. Existing C implementation still takes 66 cycles; this proposal is not implemented or synthesized. Wider SRAM improves setup bandwidth; it does not remove memory latency, wavefront fill/drain, or post-processing timing. Extra pipeline stages change these counts." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="1530" x="35" y="1000" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p6n45" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#FFF4E5;strokeColor=none;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;strokeWidth=0;" value="DESIGN CHOICE / CORAL RELATIONSHIP&lt;br&gt;Baseline keeps the existing weight-stationary array and adds native 128-bit SRAM wiring plus a tile sequencer/AGU. An optional CPU submits commands; it does not replace SRAM control or route each byte in software. Open Coral NPU instead feeds its matrix engine through vector registers and dedicated command interfaces; a full vector register file + LSU is a larger future alternative, not claimed here. AXI/TileLink may remain at the SoC boundary. No AXI protocol is required on this proposed dedicated local SRAM path. 256-bit operation needs matching banks, layout, routing and sinks. Parameter caching, hidden-vector bypass, DMA, multi-port arbitration and overlapping vectors are future extensions. References: developers.google.com/coral/guides/hardware/vme-matrix-engine and github.com/google-coral/coralnpu/blob/main/doc/overview.md." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="190" width="1530" x="35" y="1180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wide-p6-input-edge" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="E4–E5" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="110" x="35" y="290" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wide-p6-input-action" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="Read X at E4; capture low32 into x register at E5" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="760" x="145" y="290" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wide-p6-input-state" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#172B4D;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="x = [10,20,30,40]" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35" width="660" x="905" y="290" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
